.TH AENIGMA-TOR-AUTH 8 "2026-08-12" "aenigma 5.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Scripts"
.SH NAME
aenigma-tor-auth \- add Tor client authorization for an onion service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-tor-auth
.B \-s
.I SERVICE_NAME
.B \-u
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
.br
.B aenigma-tor-auth
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-tor-auth
generates a new
.B x25519
key pair and registers it as a Tor client authorization credential
for a hidden service, allowing only clients possessing the
corresponding private key to connect to that onion service.
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Generates an
.B x25519
key pair in a private, root-only temporary directory using
.BR openssl (1).
.IP \(bu 2
Extracts the raw 32-byte public and private key material from the
generated PEM files and encodes each as unpadded
.BR base32 ,
matching the format Tor expects for client authorization.
.IP \(bu 2
Writes the public half to
.IR /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth,
in the form
.BR descriptor:x25519: PUBLIC_KEY,
so that Tor will only serve descriptors for this hidden service to
clients presenting the matching private key.
.IP \(bu 2
Writes the private half to
.IR /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth.private,
which must be distributed to the authorized client and configured
in their own Tor client for them to reach the service.
.IP \(bu 2
Sets ownership of the
.I authorized_clients
directory and its contents to
.B debian-tor:debian-tor
and permissions to
.BR 700 .
.IP \(bu 2
Restarts the
.B tor
systemd service so the new authorization takes effect.
.PP
This script is also invoked automatically by
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
when its
.B \-u
option is supplied.
.PP
.B aenigma-tor-auth
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " SERVICE_NAME"
Name of the already-configured onion service (as created by
.BR aenigma-tor (8))
to add client authorization to. Required.
.TP
.BI \-u " AUTHORIZED_USER"
Identifier for the client being authorized; used as the base
filename for the generated
.I .auth
/
.I .auth.private
files. Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The authorization key pair was generated, installed, and Tor was
restarted successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or missing arguments, the script was not run as root, or
.BR openssl (1)
failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth
The public authorization credential, read by the
.B tor
daemon itself. Owned by
.B debian-tor:debian-tor
with mode
.BR 700 .
.TP
.I /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth.private
The private authorization credential. Must be securely transferred
to the authorized client and placed in their own Tor client
configuration; it is not used by the server-side
.B tor
daemon. Owned by
.B debian-tor:debian-tor
with mode
.BR 700 .
.SH EXAMPLES
Authorize a client named
.I admin
to access the
.I aenigma-dashboard
onion service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-tor-auth \-s aenigma-dashboard \-u admin
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
.B aenigma-tor-auth
does not check whether an authorization file already exists for the
given
.I SERVICE_NAME
/
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
pair before running. Re-running it for the same pair
.B silently overwrites
the existing key pair with a newly generated one; any client
already configured with the previous private key will lose access
once Tor is restarted, with no warning given.
.PP
The private authorization credential
.RI ( AUTHORIZED_USER .auth.private)
is printed to standard output as a file path at the end of a
successful run, and is written unencrypted to disk under
.IR /var/lib/tor .
Retrieval and secure delivery of this file to the intended client is
left entirely to the operator; the script provides no mechanism for
this, and the file remains root/​
.B debian-tor
readable on the server indefinitely once created.
.PP
Ownership and permissions are set with
.B chown -R
/
.B chmod -R
across the entire
.I authorized_clients
directory on every run, not just the newly created files. This
re-applies the intended ownership to all existing authorization
files for the service each time the script runs for any user, which
is generally harmless but means the script's effect is not scoped
strictly to the
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
being added.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl (1),
.BR tor (8),
.BR aenigma-tor (8),
.BR aenigma-tor-get-auth (8),
.BR base32 (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
